<title>USA: Outside panel endorses NeuroControl's Freehand.</title>
<headline>Outside panel endorses NeuroControl's Freehand.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>NeuroControl Corp said on Wednesday an outside advisory panel appointed by a division of the U.S. Food and Drug Administration recommended approval of its Freehand System.</p>
<p>NeuroControl said in a statement the U.S. FDA's Office of Device Evaluation had unanimously recommended approval of the company's neuroprosthetic implant device used to restore hand movement to people with quadriplegia.</p>
<p>The company said there were some conditions attached to the approval.</p>
<p>-- New York newsdesk 212-859-1610</p>
